[Desktop Entry]
Type=Application
Name=FirmaUY Desktop
GenericName=Firma digital
Comment=Firmá y verificá documentos con tu cédula uruguaya
Exec=firmauy-desktop
Icon=com.firmauy.firmauydesktop
Terminal=false
Categories=Office;
Keywords=firma;firmar;verificar;cédula;PAdES;XAdES;CAdES;PDF;
StartupNotify=true

# One main category, which is what desktop-file-validate asks for: Utility and Office are both
# main categories and listing two puts the application in the menu twice, while Security is an
# additional category that has to travel with Settings or System, neither of which describes an
# application for signing documents. Office does, and Keywords carries the rest of the searching.
#
# Deliberately not here yet: MimeType and an Exec that takes %F. Declaring either would put this
# application in the "open with" list for PDFs, and app.py reads no positional file out of argv,
# so a double click would open an empty window and drop the document on the floor. The association
# goes in the day the app can act on what it is handed, not before.
#
# The base name of this file is settings.APP_ID, which is also what setDesktopFileName reports, so
# the compositor can tie a window to this entry rather than guess. A test holds the three together.
